{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21687 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a mechanistic link between the compound 8-methoxy-2-phenyl-5-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromen-4-one and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, all of which are known to interact with macrophage scavenger receptors I and II. These receptors are known to be targets of (Z)-Calacorene, Macaflavone II, and [3-(3-Hydroxy-4,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-3-oxopropyl] acetate, all of which are implicated in modulating the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The shared target of these compounds, macrophage scavenger receptors, implies a potential mechanism by which the compound may influence the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence is consistent with a pathway where the compound may act through interactions with these receptors, potentially modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The presence of multiple compounds with overlapping targets supports the hypothesis that the compound may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving macrophage scavenger receptors.",
